# Relationships and Program

## Refined Question

The original question "which activities depend on which, and which can run at the same time?" misses critical timing constraints that the text implies:

**Better question:** Which activities must finish at a specific moment to meet the 09:00 deadline? Which must rest, cool, or be held warm while other work proceeds? Which depend on a resource becoming available (griddle cleaned, batter rested, coffee fresh)? Which must start at a precise offset from another (toast when the last pancake pass starts; grinder 10 minutes after bacon finishes)? Which activities can overlap only if they use different resources?

This exposes:
- **Rest dependencies**: pancake batter must rest 20 minutes after mixing before griddle cooking can begin.
- **Holding indefinitely**: plates in the oven stay warm throughout the entire program until `serve` ends it.
- **Synchronization at finish**: eggs, toast, and coffee must ALL be ready at the same moment so `serve` can begin.
- **Precise offset**: grinder starts exactly 10 minutes after bacon begins (not after bacon ends).
- **Toast trigger**: first toast batch starts when the last (third) pancake pass goes on the griddle.
- **Sequential griddle work**: each phase (heat, bacon, clean, pancakes 1–3, cool, eggs) must complete before the next.

---

## Track Assignments

| Track | Purpose | Steps |
|-------|---------|-------|
| **griddle-line** | Griddle cooking (primary bottleneck) | heat-griddle, cook-bacon, clean-griddle, pancakes-pass-1, pancakes-pass-2, pancakes-pass-3, cool-griddle, scramble-eggs |
| **pancake-prep** | Pancake batter prep and rest | mix-pancake-batter, rest-pancake-batter |
| **egg-prep** | Egg prep | prep-eggs |
| **table-prep** | Table setting | set-table |
| **toast-line** | Toast (two-slice toaster, parallel with griddle) | toast-batch-1, toast-batch-2, butter-toast |
| **coffee-line** | Grinder and coffee maker (starts at precise offset from bacon) | grind-beans, brew-coffee |
| **oven-line** | Warm plates and hold finished items | warm-plates |
| **serve-line** | Final synchronization and service | serve |

---

## Trigger Logic

- **pancake-prep**: `mix-pancake-batter` starts at `programStart`; `rest-pancake-batter` starts `afterStep: mix-pancake-batter`.
- **griddle-line**: `heat-griddle` starts at `programStart`. `cook-bacon` starts after heat-griddle ends. `clean-griddle` starts after bacon ends. `pancakes-pass-1` starts when both clean-griddle ends AND rest-pancake-batter ends — use `compound` with `"logic": "all"`.
- **toast-line**: `toast-batch-1` starts when `pancakes-pass-3` begins (not when it ends) — use `afterStep` with `"event": "start"`. `toast-batch-2` chains after `toast-batch-1`. `butter-toast` chains after `toast-batch-2`.
- **coffee-line**: `grind-beans` starts 10 minutes (600 seconds) after `cook-bacon` **starts** — use `afterStep: cook-bacon` with `"event": "start"` and `"offsetSeconds": 600`. `brew-coffee` chains after `grind-beans`.
- **oven-line**: `warm-plates` starts at `programStart` and runs indefinite (until `serve` pulls them out).
- **serve-line**: `serve` starts when all three finish lines (eggs, toast, coffee) are ready — use `compound` with `"logic": "all"` and `afterStep` triggers for `scramble-eggs`, `butter-toast`, and `brew-coffee`.

